From 437613940df9cfd0a2d51c6e56397c7517c6f141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The ancient spellbook is Jagex's panel now, not a
 reconstruction

scripts/interfaces/inter_267.if IS the 377 cache's Ancient Magicks interface. It sat
unrecognised because an unpacked interface contains no word you would grep for - every
component is com_<n> - while ancient_magic.if was rebuilt by hand beside it, its own
header saying the real coordinates "are not in this checkout". They were.

What the swap gains is the picture: Jagex's interleaved layout instead of a 4x4 block,
and the bordered description panel under the grid that the hover text draws into - four
nested rects, the only four components the reconstruction had no counterpart for.

What it does NOT gain, measured rather than assumed: the two files carry 760 script
operands, 180 staff checks, 278 rune-pouch reads and 73 rune models EACH. The
reconstruction was a faithful copy of the logic. An earlier draft of this comment
claimed the cache panel had longer staff lists; it does not, and counting said so.

The rename is a join on each button's magicoff2 sprite index, checked against the
cache's own action= text for the sixteen it names. The battery checks it a third way
that nothing here wrote: every tooltip's "Level 94 : Ice Barrage" against that spell's
levelrequired in magic_spell_table. All 24 agree.

The eight teleports' option= strings are the one thing that is not the cache's - the
real panel has none, which packs as a blank right-click row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015mjzJ5S7cQ1h1aE5KeBabD
